      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin in adults. At that dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't change the labeled limit.\n\nHere are some options within the label:\n\n- **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **Metformin 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day, a common target dose.\n- **Metformin 500 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is a typical starting dose, which you can titrate up.\n\nIf 1700 mg was meant to be the total daily dose, for example 850 mg twice daily, tell me and I'll enter that. If you meant a different dose or frequency, give me the details and I'll enter it."
      }
